## Interface and Type Documentation

### 🔄 Update Trigger: EVERY time interfaces/types are created, properties added/removed, or usage changes

### Interface Documentation
Document all exported interfaces with TypeDoc-specific features:

```typescript
/**
 * Configuration options for text-to-speech conversion
 * 
 * This interface defines all available options for customizing TTS output,
 * including voice selection, audio format, and speech parameters.
 * 
 * @example
 * ```typescript
 * const config: TtsConfig = {
 *   voice: 'en-US-Standard-A',
 *   audioFormat: 'mp3',
 *   speed: 1.0,
 *   pitch: 0
 * };
 * ```
 * 
 * @category Configuration
 */
export interface TtsConfig {
  /**
   * Voice identifier for speech synthesis
   * @see {@link VoiceList.getVoices} for available voices
   */
  voice: string;
  
  /**
   * Output audio format
   * @defaultValue 'mp3'
   */
  audioFormat?: AudioFormat;
  
  /**
   * Speech speed multiplier
   * @remarks Must be between 0.25 and 4.0
   * @defaultValue 1.0
   */
  speed?: number;
}
```

### Type Alias Documentation
Document complex type aliases with usage context:

```typescript
/**
 * Supported audio output formats across all TTS providers
 * 
 * Each provider may support different subsets of these formats.
 * Use {@link AudioCapabilities.getSupportedFormats} to check provider-specific support.
 * 
 * @category Audio Processing
 */
export type AudioFormat = 'mp3' | 'wav' | 'ogg' | 'flac';

/**
 * Union type representing all possible TTS error types
 * 
 * @category Error Handling
 */
export type TtsErrorType = 
  | TtsAuthenticationError 
  | TtsRateLimitError 
  | TtsValidationError 
  | TtsNetworkError;
```

## Error Handling Documentation

### Error Class Documentation
Document custom error classes with TypeDoc-specific error handling:

```typescript
/**
 * Base error class for all Text-to-Speech operations
 * 
 * Provides standardized error handling with retry information,
 * provider context, and user-friendly error messages.
 * 
 * @example Catching and Handling TTS Errors
 * ```typescript
 * try {
 *   const audio = await tts.convert('Hello world');
 * } catch (error) {
 *   if (error instanceof TtsError) {
 *     console.error(`Error: ${error.getUserMessage()}`);
 *     
 *     if (error.retryable) {
 *       // Implement retry logic
 *       console.log('Error is retryable, attempting again...');
 *     }
 *   }
 * }
 * ```
 * 
 * @example Creating Custom TTS Errors
 * ```typescript
 * throw new TtsError(
 *   'Voice not found',
 *   TtsErrorCode.INVALID_VOICE,
 *   {
 *     provider: 'google',
 *     retryable: false,
 *     context: { voiceId: 'invalid-voice-id' }
 *   }
 * );
 * ```
 * 
 * @category Error Handling
 */
export class TtsError extends Error {
  /**
   * Standardized error code for programmatic handling
   * @readonly
   */
  public readonly code: TtsErrorCode;
  
  /**
   * Whether this error condition can be retried
   * @readonly
   */
  public readonly retryable: boolean;
}
```

## TypeDoc-Specific Tags and Features

### Required TypeDoc Tags
Use these TypeDoc-specific tags for better documentation generation:

```typescript
/**
 * Method description
 * 
 * @param param - Parameter description
 * @returns Return description
 * @throws {ErrorType} Error description with {@link ErrorType} link
 * @example Example with proper syntax highlighting
 * @since Version information
 * @deprecated Use {@link NewMethod} instead
 * @see {@link RelatedClass} or {@link https://external-link.com | External Link}
 * @category Category Name
 * @internal For internal APIs not shown in public docs
 * @readonly For readonly properties
 * @defaultValue For default parameter values
 * @remarks Additional important information
 * @typeParam T - Description of generic type parameter
 */
```

### Generic Type Documentation
Document generic types and constraints:

```typescript
/**
 * Generic cache implementation with automatic expiration
 * 
 * @template T - The type of data being cached
 * @template K - The type of cache keys, defaults to string
 * 
 * @example
 * ```typescript
 * // Cache voice data with string keys
 * const voiceCache = new Cache<VoiceData>();
 * 
 * // Cache with custom key type
 * const customCache = new Cache<UserData, number>();
 * ```
 * 
 * @category Common Utilities
 */
export class Cache<T, K extends string | number = string> {
  /**
   * Stores an item in the cache with optional TTL
   * 
   * @param key - Cache key of type K
   * @param value - Value to cache of type T
   * @param ttl - Time to live in milliseconds
   * @typeParam T - Type of the cached value
   * @typeParam K - Type of the cache key
   */
  set(key: K, value: T, ttl?: number): void {
  }
}
```

## Code Examples Standards

### Example Quality Requirements
All `@example` tags must contain:
- **Working code** that can be copy-pasted and run
- **Proper imports** when necessary
- **Error handling** for complex examples
- **Comments** explaining key steps
- **Multiple examples** for complex methods (basic + advanced)

### Example Template
```typescript
/**
 * Method description
 * 
 * @example Basic Usage
 * ```typescript
 * import { TtsUniversal } from 'cloud-text-to-speech';
 * 
 * // Initialize TTS
 * TtsUniversal.init({
 *   provider: 'google',
 *   googleParams: { apiKey: 'your-api-key' }
 * });
 * 
 * // Convert text to speech
 * const result = await TtsUniversal.convertTts({
 *   text: 'Hello world',
 *   voice: { name: 'en-US-Standard-A' }
 * });
 * 
 * console.log(`Generated ${result.audio.length} bytes of audio`);
 * ```
 * 
 * @example Advanced Usage with Error Handling
 * ```typescript
 * try {
 *   const result = await TtsUniversal.convertTts({
 *     text: 'Complex text with SSML <break time="1s"/> pauses',
 *     voice: { 
 *       name: 'en-US-Neural2-A',
 *       provider: 'google'
 *     },
 *     audioConfig: {
 *       audioEncoding: 'MP3',
 *       speakingRate: 1.2,
 *       pitch: 2.0
 *     }
 *   });
 *   
 *   // Save audio to file
 *   await fs.writeFile('output.mp3', result.audio);
 *   console.log('Audio saved successfully');
 *   
 * } catch (error) {
 *   if (error instanceof TtsRateLimitError) {
 *     console.log(`Rate limited, retry after ${error.retryAfter} seconds`);
 *   } else if (error instanceof TtsAuthenticationError) {
 *     console.error('Authentication failed, check your API key');
 *   }
 * }
 * ```
 */
```

## Inline Code Documentation Standards

### 🔄 Update Trigger: EVERY time code logic is added, modified, refactored, or optimized

### Single-Line Comments for Complex Logic
Use clear, descriptive comments for complex algorithms and business logic:

```typescript
// Cache hit: return cached data if not expired
if (cached && Date.now() - cached.timestamp < cached.ttl) {
    return cached.data;
}

// Apply exponential backoff with jitter to prevent thundering herd
const baseDelay = Math.min(1000 * Math.pow(2, attempt), this.maxDelay);
const jitteredDelay = baseDelay * (0.5 + Math.random() * 0.5);

// Provider-specific rate limit headers take precedence over calculated delay
if (error.retryAfter && error.retryAfter > jitteredDelay / 1000) {
    return error.retryAfter * 1000;
}
```

### Comment Style Guidelines
- Place comments **above** the code they describe
- Use comments to explain **why** and **how**, not **what**
- Keep comments concise but descriptive
- Update comments when refactoring code
- Use proper grammar and punctuation

## File Header Standards

### 🔄 Update Trigger: EVERY time a new file is created or a file's purpose/functionality significantly changes

### Mandatory TypeDoc File Headers
**ALL TypeScript files MUST start with a comprehensive `@fileoverview` section** before any imports or code. This is not optional - it's required for generating proper API documentation.

### Complete File Header Template
Every TypeScript file must include:

```typescript
/**
 * @fileoverview [Brief description of module purpose and functionality]
 * 
 * [Detailed description explaining what the module does, its main responsibilities,
 * key features, and how it integrates with other parts of the system. Include
 * information about supported providers, algorithms, or patterns used.]
 * 
 * [Additional context about the module's role in the larger system, any important
 * architectural decisions, or performance considerations.]
 * 
 * @author Marko Kostich
 * @since [version when module was introduced]
 * @see {@link https://github.com/markokosticdev/cloud_text_to_speech_nodejs | GitHub Repository}
 * @see {@link RelatedInterface} for related functionality
 * @see {@link https://external-docs.com | External Documentation}
 * 
 * @example Basic usage example
 * ```typescript
 * import { MainClass } from './module.js';
 * 
 * // Initialize and use the main functionality
 * const instance = new MainClass(config);
 * const result = await instance.primaryMethod();
 * console.log(result);
 * ```
 * 
 * @example Advanced usage with error handling
 * ```typescript
 * import { MainClass, ErrorType } from './module.js';
 * 
 * try {
 *   const instance = new MainClass({
 *     option1: 'value1',
 *     option2: 'value2'
 *   });
 *   
 *   const result = await instance.complexMethod(parameters);
 *   // Handle successful result
 * } catch (error) {
 *   if (error instanceof ErrorType) {
 *     console.error('Specific error handling');
 *   }
 * }
 * ```
 * 
 * @example Integration with other modules
 * ```typescript
 * import { MainClass } from './module.js';
 * import { HelperModule } from '../helpers/helper.js';
 * 
 * // Show how this module integrates with others
 * const helper = new HelperModule();
 * const main = new MainClass(helper.getConfig());
 * 
 * const combined = await main.useWith(helper);
 * ```
 * 
 * @example Production deployment pattern
 * ```typescript
 * // Show real-world usage patterns
 * const productionConfig = {
 *   provider: 'google',
 *   timeout: 30000,
 *   retries: 3
 * };
 * 
 * const service = new MainClass(productionConfig);
 * 
 * // Production error handling
 * service.on('error', (error) => {
 *   logger.error('Service error:', error);
 * });
 * 
 * await service.start();
 * ```
 */
```

