### File Header Quality Standards

#### Required Elements
- **Clear module purpose** - One sentence summary + detailed description
- **Author information** - Always "Marko Kostich"
- **Version information** - `@since` tag with version
- **GitHub repository link** - Standard link format
- **Related documentation** - Links to provider docs, RFCs, specifications
- **Multiple working examples** - At least 2-4 comprehensive examples
- **Cross-references** - Links to related modules and interfaces

#### Example Requirements
- **Basic usage** - Simple, copy-paste ready example
- **Advanced usage** - Complex scenario with error handling
- **Integration** - How module works with other parts
- **Production patterns** - Real-world deployment examples
- **All examples must be runnable** - Include necessary imports and setup

### File Header Validation
- **Required for all .ts files** - No exceptions
- **Must be first thing in file** - Before any imports
- **Must include working examples** - Validated during build
- **Must have proper cross-references** - Links validated
- **Must match module's actual functionality** - Reviewed in PR

### Common File Header Mistakes to Avoid
❌ **Missing @fileoverview entirely**
❌ **Generic or copy-pasted descriptions**
❌ **Examples that don't work or lack imports**
❌ **Missing @since version information**
❌ **No cross-references to related modules**
❌ **Single basic example instead of comprehensive coverage**
❌ **Descriptions that don't match actual code functionality**

✅ **Complete, module-specific documentation**
✅ **Multiple working examples covering different scenarios**
✅ **Proper version and authorship information**
✅ **Extensive cross-references and external links**
✅ **Production-ready examples and patterns**
✅ **Clear integration guidance**

## Enforcement & TypeDoc Integration

### TypeDoc Configuration Requirements
Your `typedoc.json` must include:
- Proper categorization with `categorizeByGroup: true`
- Validation settings for documentation completeness
- GitHub integration for source links
- Search functionality with `searchInComments: true`

### Code Review Checklist
**Every pull request MUST verify:**
- [ ] All new classes have class-level TypeDoc comments with `@category` tags
- [ ] All new/modified public methods have comprehensive TypeDoc documentation
- [ ] All `@example` tags contain working, runnable code
- [ ] Method signatures match the documented parameters and return types
- [ ] Error conditions are documented with `@throws` tags linking to specific error types
- [ ] Generic types include `@typeParam` documentation
- [ ] Complex logic has explanatory inline comments
- [ ] Generated TypeDoc HTML is reviewed for accuracy and completeness

### Automated TypeDoc Validation
```bash
# Generate documentation and check for issues
npm run docs:html

# Validate documentation coverage
npm run docs:coverage

# Test all code examples in documentation
npm run docs:test-examples

# Watch for changes and regenerate docs
npm run docs:watch

# Serve documentation locally for review
npm run docs:serve
```

### Quality Standards for TypeDoc Output
- **Navigation clarity** - Proper categorization for easy browsing
- **Search functionality** - All content searchable including comments
- **Cross-references** - Extensive use of `{@link}` tags for related items
- **Working examples** - All examples must be tested and functional
- **Visual hierarchy** - Proper use of headings, lists, and code blocks
- **Mobile-friendly** - Documentation must be readable on all devices

### TypeDoc Documentation Debt Prevention
- **Block merges** if TypeDoc generation fails or produces warnings
- **Require category assignment** for all public classes and interfaces
- **Mandate working examples** for all public APIs
- **Enforce link validation** to ensure all `{@link}` references are valid
- **Check example syntax** to ensure all code examples have proper syntax highlighting

**Remember: TypeDoc documentation is the primary way users will interact with your API. High-quality TypeDoc comments directly translate to professional, comprehensive documentation websites that users can easily navigate and understand.**
